# Always deploy after changes

When cloud code, templates, or static files change, ship them in the same turn. Do not wait for the user to say deploy.

1. Commit the product files (never `ewnext.db`, `.env`, passwords, cookies, API keys, or DB credentials).
2. `git push origin HEAD` to GitHub `RichardChitambo2312/ewnext-cloud` `main`.
3. Render auto-deploy is off. Open `ewnext-cloud` (`srv-dbc8egdg1s2s739d71v0`) → Manual Deploy → Deploy latest commit.
4. Wait until the deploy is live, then tell the user to hard-refresh `https://ewnext-cloud.onrender.com`.

Router/UCI work is separate: do not reboot the TRB245 unless the user approves.
